From 68b7647d1a90ceb83469f338061ee72e9a145fe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason chien <3936511+jason5545@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:35:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] steamac: share textures through host memory without Win32
 handle export

CrossOver on macOS (KosmicKrisp behind CrossOver 27 Wine) exposes no
VK_KHR_external_memory_win32 to applications, but does expose
VK_EXT_external_memory_host. On such devices, shared D3D11 textures now
live in a pagefile-backed section: a header at offset 0 (description,
row pitch) and a LINEAR image from 64 KiB on, imported into the VkDevice
with VK_EXT_external_memory_host. The NT handle is a new handle to the
section, the KMT handle is the section handle itself. vkd3d-proton
(jason5545/vkd3d-proton-steamac) uses the same layout, so D3D11 and D3D12
can open each other's textures.

- VK_EXT_external_memory_host is only enabled on devices without
  VK_KHR_external_memory_win32; elsewhere nothing changes.
- Shared textures that host memory cannot back (mips, arrays, MSAA,
  multi-planar, depth-stencil, unsupported LINEAR usage) fail to create
  instead of being created unshared.
- The section view is unmapped in ~DxvkResourceAllocation after
  vkFreeMemory, so it outlives GPU use.
- Keyed mutex: keys are not enforced (no cross-device semaphore);
  ReleaseSync waits for the GPU to finish with the texture.
- STEAMAC_NO_HOST_SHARING=1 disables the path.
